`python3 test_all.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress 1.1s). I fixed four bugs and left `test_all.py` untouched:

- **`stats.py` `mean`**: divided by `len(xs) - 1`; it now divides by `len(xs)`. This also fixes `variance`, which depends on it.
- **`stats.py` `median`**: for even-length input it returned the upper middle element; it now averages the two middle elements.
- **`seq.py` `dedup`**: it appended the duplicates and dropped the first occurrences; it now keeps each first-seen item in order.
- **`textproc.py` `top_words`**: it ranked alphabetically by word rather than by count; it now sorts by count descending, with ties broken alphabetically.

The suite did not catch the `top_words` bug: its only test case (`"x x x y y z"`) happens to give the same answer either way, so the suite already passed after the first three fixes. I fixed it anyway and confirmed with a separate check (`'a b b c c c'` → `['c', 'b']`). The alphabetical tie-break is my choice, since the tests don't specify one.
